===================Base convertion================================
1 .Any base to base 10 : use this formula (base to the power of position)

  (213)10 =>  2  1      0
            10  10      10 (base)
            2    1      0(pos)
            2    1      3  
  ---------------------------------
            2*10^2 + 1*10^1  + 3*10^0 (base to the power of position)
            200 + 10 + 3 = (213)10
  ---------------------------------
  
  (36)10 convert to base 2 =?  36/2 => 18/2 => 9/2 => 4/2 => 2/2 => 1/2   
             Reminder           0        0      1      0      0       1
  36 base 2   => (100100)2

2. base 10 to any ither base:

*k^i                                                     / p
base-k ---------------> base-10 ------------------------>base-p

Base-p -------------->base-10---------------------------> base-k
*p^1                                                    / k

TC -> time complexity of this base conversion => O(log N). no of digit is log of N

